<div class="alert alert-warning border-warning" role="alert" id="whatsapp-risk-warning">
    <div class="fw-semibold mb-1">⚠ Read this before connecting a WhatsApp number</div>
    <p class="mb-2 small">WAHA automates <strong>WhatsApp Web</strong>. It is <strong>not</strong> the official WhatsApp Business Platform. WhatsApp can <strong>restrict or permanently ban</strong> a number that sends unwanted or bulk messages, without warning and without a way to appeal through us. Sessions can also drop and need a new QR scan.</p>
    <ul class="small mb-0">
        <li>Use a number you can afford to lose. Do not use your main business line.</li>
        <li>Message only people who agreed to hear from you, and only reply to people who write to you wherever possible. WAHA's own guidance is to never start conversations in bulk.</li>
        <li>LeadPilot enforces conservative limits (hourly and daily caps, minimum gap between messages, warm-up from 20 messages on day one), checks consent and the suppression list before every send, treats a STOP message as an immediate opt-out, and pauses the account automatically when sends keep failing or WhatsApp restricts it. These limits reduce the risk; they cannot remove it.</li>
        <li>For bulk or cold marketing the official Business Platform is the right tool.</li>
    </ul>
</div>
